invariant: INV-22
file: srv_quic.c
catches: quic_loop_test
reason: the QUIC server completes on a client Finished that has more bytes
  after it in the same Handshake delivery. srv_complete empties cfg.buf, so
  drive's check never sees the bytes, and a KeyUpdate that RFC 9001 section
  6 makes 0x010a is dropped while the server reports CH_ST_CONNECTED.
  colibri found it with h3spec. test/quic_loop_close.h delivers a Finished
  and a KeyUpdate in one call and requires 0x010a and no ticket.

--- old
    if (q->t.pt_off != q->t.pt_len) {
        return quic_refuse_unread(q);
    }
--- new
    (void)quic_refuse_unread;
